{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider asked for this detour herself. MSG-00109-001 in the chat log was sent by RIDER at 18:22:06, roughly a minute after the meter started at 18:21:10, and reads 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min'; the platform resolved that message to a waypoint_hint of Jurong Point PHV Pickup Point, 1 Jurong West Central 2 (VEN-JURONG-POINT). That satisfies every limb of POL-RD-04: the instruction comes from the rider, it is timestamped before the vehicle left the optimal corridor rather than more than three minutes after, and it names a place specifically enough to act on. The driver accepted it thirteen seconds later with 'ok can, i wait at the phv pickup point'.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[MSG-00109-001].waypoint_hint",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace corroborates the requested stop, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test is run and passed rather than undecidable. EV-GPS-00109 is unbroken 10-second telemetry with 100% coverage, 207 fixes and max_gap_sec of 0.0, and its admissibility assessment records the vehicle stationary 38 m from the Jurong Point PHV pickup point named in the rider's own message for 366 seconds, well inside the 200 m corroboration radius the clause requires. The same trace lists a 0.0 km/h speed sample among its distinct speeds, which is a vehicle waiting at a pickup point, not a vehicle driving past one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the detour was rider-caused, the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied, as POL-RD-04 expressly directs. The derived deviation block measures 7.36 km of excess at 115.00% of an optimal of 6.4 km, but that block is itself computed on the raw trace total (trace_distance_km 13.76 against optimal_distance_km 6.4) and takes no account of the exclusion the clause requires. Once the rider-requested Jurong Point leg is removed, the deviation gate in POL-RD-01 is not met and no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No residual excess above the POL-RD-01 threshold is shown on this record. The 7.36 km and 115.00% figures are unadjusted totals; nothing in the derived block, the trip record or the fare breakdown isolates a post-exclusion excess, and under POL-RD-08 the rider carries the burden of proving an excess measured after the rider-caused leg comes out. A materiality figure computed before the adjustment the governing clause mandates cannot discharge that burden.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-06 profile check comes back clean and no uplift or referral is available on it. Even if the judge treats a material deviation as recorded, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 511, a ratio of 0.00, far below the 0.05 with at least 40 completed trips that POL-RD-06 requires before a pattern is established. No pattern means no limb (a) tilt of a balanced record, no limb (b) uplift of the contested SGD 21.32 to a FULL_REFUND, and no limb (c) conduct referral. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the trailing-90-day field the clause names and cannot be substituted for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver is owed compensation for distance the platform never billed. fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km is 9.60 while the governing gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 13.76, a shortfall of 4.16 km that exceeds the 1.0 km gate in POL-RD-04's compensation limb. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is 3.12, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 as SGD 3.15, comfortably inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. The payments artifact flags the shortfall itself as a substantive POL-RD-04 finding, not a cross-source data error.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.distance_charge",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory exists for this trip and the driver does not need one: EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING from the pool, carries no payload, and has admissibility weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so no POL-RD-03 closure exoneration is asserted or available. The absence is citable and it is the platform's own assessment that 'the detour is explained by the rider's own instruction, not by any road condition' — which is precisely the POL-RD-04 route the driver relies on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00109-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.issues",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through money to correct on top. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries and erp_lines total 0.00, no tolls, an airport surcharge of 0.00 on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, no promo discount and no waiting-time fee, so POL-RD-09 gives the rider nothing to add to the contested amount. The only contested money is the distance and time charge on the trip the rider herself asked to be extended.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the rider's claim the present state stands, and the outcome this case produces is compensation to the driver. fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00; with POL-RD-04 exonerating the detour there is no POL-RD-02 recomputation to displace that charge, and under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute leaves the charge exactly as it is rather than restoring or increasing it. The ruling should therefore be DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.15, with amount_sgd carrying that same figure, no refund to the rider, and no referral, since POL-RD-06(c) is not triggered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION","amount_sgd":3.15,"driver_compensation_sgd":3.15,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"To the rider: your trip ran 13.76 km on the GPS trace (the governing field) against a booked optimal of 6.4 km — an excess of 7.36 km, or 115%. Normally that would be refundable. It is not here, because you asked for it. Your message at 18:22:06, one minute after the meter started, read 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', and the platform saved Jurong Point PHV Pickup Point as the message's waypoint. The driver agreed at 18:22:31. The trace shows the car standing 38 m from that waypoint for 366 seconds — about six minutes, matching the driver's account — and the furthest point the car reached from your pickup, 7.09 km, is the distance to Jurong Point, so the route was Clementi → Jurong Point → Bukit Batok. POL-RD-04 excludes the distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor, and here that is the whole of the 7.36 km excess. No deviation therefore stands, and the $21.32 charge stays: the $12.00 you contested is not refunded. Your argument that no separate post-exclusion figure appears in the file is noted but rejected — the exclusion is run on the artifacts themselves (the message, its stored waypoint, and the trace's own path), and on that path nothing is left over. The $21.32 charged_total and the $13.32 recomputed fare are therefore not used, because POL-RD-02 never runs.

To the driver: for the same reason the distance and time charges stand. Separately, the fare breakdown billed 9.60 km while the trace records 13.76 km driven, so 4.16 km went unpaid. POL-RD-04 pays SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre: 4.16 × 0.75 = $3.12, rounded up to $3.15, well under the $15.00 per-trip cap. The ruling orders $3.15 to you, and that same figure is recorded as the amount the ruling moves.

For both: no traffic advisory covers this trip — the advisory artifact is missing, weight 0.0, which is noted but exonerates nothing, so POL-RD-03 gives no relief. There are no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines on the fare breakdown, so no pass-through correction arises under POL-RD-09. On the driver's profile, deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 511 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and no driver-conduct referral is made. The rider's claim history (1 deviation claim in 60 days) does not trigger the extra-corroboration rule and did not affect the outcome. The trace is unimpaired (207 fixes, 10-second interval, no gaps), so nothing escalates. Every artifact that decides this case carries weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0; confidence is 0.9."},"discarded_claims":[]}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.15,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver — this is a route-deviation dispute over trip TRP-00109 (Clementi MRT to Bukit Batok MRT), charged at SGD 21.32. The outcome is DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.15.\n\n1. The deviation the rider measures is real on the raw trace, but it is rider-caused. The GPS trace records 13.76 km driven against a 6.4 km booked optimal — an excess of 7.36 km, 115%, which clears both POL-RD-01 gates and is material (trace-derived status 'material'). On that alone the rider's arithmetic would be a PARTIAL_REFUND: charged_total 21.32 less a recomputed fare of 13.32 (base 3.80 + 0.75 x 6.4 km + 0.28 x 14.0 min, surge multiplier 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + 0.80 platform fee), giving 8.00, above the 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share. That is the figure the rider asks me to award.\n\n2. POL-RD-04 displaces it. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00109) shows MSG-00109-001, sent by the RIDER at 18:22:06 — about a minute after the trip started at 18:21:10, well inside the 3-minute window — reading 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', which the platform resolved to a specific place, the Jurong Point PHV Pickup Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT) carried on the message's waypoint_hint. The driver accepted 25 seconds later. The corroboration limb is satisfied on the field the clause requires: the clean 10-second, 207-fix, zero-gap trace puts the vehicle stationary 38 m from that waypoint for 366 seconds, inside the 200 m radius. Every limb of POL-RD-04 passes, the clause is available (not undecidable), and the excess attributable to the requested Jurong Point stop is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 run. The booked optimal runs Clementi Road to Bukit Batok East Ave 3; Jurong Point lies off that corridor in the opposite direction, so the whole of the 7.36 km excess is attributable to the stop the rider asked for. No deviation survives the exclusion and no distance-or-time refund is due. The rider's POL-RD-01, POL-RD-02 and POL-RD-08 claims all fail at this point — the raw excess they measure is the unadjusted figure the clause requires me to adjust — and her 8.00 claim is rejected.\n\n3. The driver is owed for distance the platform never billed. fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km is 9.60 against the trace's 13.76 km — a shortfall of 4.16 km, above the 1.0 km gate in POL-RD-04's compensation limb. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is 3.12, rounded UP to SGD 3.15, inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. That limb is granted.\n\n4. Everything else falls away. EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT); its absence carries no fact and no POL-RD-03 closure exoneration is asserted or available — the rider's point that the driver has no road-condition answer is correct and does not help her. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries, no tolls, zero airport surcharge, no promo and no waiting-time fee, so POL-RD-09 gives nothing to either side. The driver's profile shows no repeat pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 511, a ratio of 0.00, far below the 0.05 / 40-trip test), so no POL-RD-06 limb (a) tilt, no limb (b) uplift to FULL_REFUND and no limb (c) conduct referral — both advocates agree on this and I confirm it. The profile fields raised in argument (rider rating, account age, lifetime trips, prior disputes; driver prior_deviation_flags) are context-only under POL-GEN-01 and are correctly not used as grounds by either side; no claim was discarded for that reason. POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply (no amendment timestamps and amended_optimal_distance_km null; vehicle_type RYDE_X not RYDE_POOL). The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (max gap 0 s, sampling 10 s, no jumps), so no corroboration requirement or confidence cap arises from impairment, and the only sub-1.0 artifact in the pool is the missing advisory, which carries no fact. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers and pickup timestamps match, no timestamp disagreement, no missing field behind an invoked exculpatory clause, no unmatched charge line, and no comparable-strength contradiction — the GPS corroborates the rider's own request rather than contradicting it.\n\n5. Under POL-GEN-03 a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling carries the same figure in amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd: SGD 3.15. The rider's charge stands as billed (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). Figures used: charged_total 21.32; recomputed fare 13.32; billed distance 9.60 km; trace distance 13.76 km; shortfall 4.16 km; 4.16 x 0.75 = 3.12 rounded up to 3.15. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
